nfo\": {...}}`, and print_serial is called with `data[\"info\"]`... that's what the code does. Hmm.\n\nLet me just run the test after applying the patch and see. Actually — wait. Let me recheck: is it possible that `name` and `folder` are printed and then \"packages\" list items... Let me just run the tests and observe the actual output.\n\nActually hold on, let me reconsider print_serial indentation:\n\n```python\ndef print_serial(item, indent=None, color_index=None):\n    indent = \"\" if indent is None else (indent + \"  \")\n```\n\nTop call: indent=None → indent=\"\". For dict at top: writes f\"{indent}{k}\" = \"packages\" — wait no. Top call is print_serial(data[\"info\"]) with indent=None → indent = \"\" (because indent is None → \"\"). So keys at top level get written with indent \"\" → \"name: ...\", \"folder: ...\", \"packages\" (no leading spaces!).\n\nI misread: `indent = \"\" if indent is None else (indent + \"  \")` — top-level indent is \"\", not \"  \". Then for the list recursion, indent = \"\" + \"  \" = \"  \" → items at 2 spaces: \"  - path: ../liba\", \"    ref: liba/0.1\" (elem has its own 2 spaces).\n\nSo actual output:\n```\nname: mywks\nfolder: ...\npackages\n  - path: ../liba\n    ref: liba/0.1\n  - path: ../app1\n    ref: app1/0.1\n```\n\nAnd expected = \"packages\\n  - path: ../liba\\n    ref: liba/0.1\\n  - path: ../app1\\n    ref: app1/0.1\\n\" — a substring. \n\nAnd for `test_workspace_defining_only_paths`:\n```\npackages\n  - path: liba\n  - path: libb\n  - path: app1\n```\nmatches too (no refs since conanws.yml has no refs — note `info()` uses `self._ws.packages()` raw data, so paths stay relative as written in the yml).\n\nNow let me fix the `remove()` StopIteration bug and then run the tests.","signature":""}],"model":"z-ai/glm-5.3-flash","stop_reason":null,"stop_details":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0,"output_tokens_details":null,"cache_creation_input_tokens":null,"cache_read_input_tokens":nul