{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"gen-1788513510-NgxCdBUQB2iuookrCFf8","type":"message","role":"assistant","container":null,"content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Very good progress. Everything works:\n- yml is now a list: `packages: [- output_folder: build/liba, path: liba, ref: liba/0.1, - path: libb, ref: libb/0.1]`\n- duplicate path add → warning + skip (need to see the warning message — it printed \"Reference 'libb/0.1' added to workspace\" from CLI plus warning? Let me check the earlier output... The output for the third add was cut off before \"===== conanws.yml after adds =====\". Actually the output shows everything but I didn't see the \"already exists, skipping\" warning — it's before the first ===== line. The output starts with \"===== conanws.yml after adds =====\" — hmm, the first lines (from the three adds) aren't shown? Looking at the output, it starts with \"===== conanws.yml after adds =====\". The add outputs (WARN: Workspace found, Reference added) should have appeared first... The captured output above begins with \"===== conanws.yml after adds =====\" — wait no, there's a portion at the top: actually the traceback is at line 27 (`workspace info` with assert_error). The add messages... I see \"WARN: Workspace found:\" lines only inside later outputs. The first add outputs seem missing from the captured output — possibly buffered/trimmed. Not critical; the duplicate detection warning wasn't displayed though. Let me check specifically.\n\nOne issue found in the smoke: `workspace info` with a package whose ref cannot be deduced did NOT error — it printed the info fine. Wait, why? The saved conanws.yml is `packages:\\n  - path: nocall` where nocall/conanfile.py is empty (no name/version). `workspace info` succeeded!\n\nHmm — why? `info()` in the API returns `self._ws.packages()` — the RAW list, without going through the validation in `WorkspaceAPI.packages()`. So `workspace info` (text/json) doesn't validate refs — matches upstream #18493 behavior (the info command shows raw paths; the test `test_workspace_defining_only_paths` expects info to work with only paths, and `workspace install` is what triggers reference deduction). My smoke script wrongly asserted an error there — that assertion is my own, not from upstream. So this is expected behavior: info doesn't deduce refs; install/build do.\n\nLet me rerun the remaining part of the smoke (duplicate ref, missing path) and also verify the duplicate-path warning message and the \"undeducible ref\" error via `workspace install`.","signature":""}],"model":"z-ai/glm-5.3-flash","stop_reason":null,"stop_details":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0,"output_tokens_details":null,"cache_creation_input_tokens":null,"cache_read_input_tokens":null,"cache_creation":null,"inference_geo":null,"server_tool_use":null,"service_tier":null,"speed":"standard"},"provider":"Parasail","context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a035cbe5-8923-4731-8824-502460b30912","uuid":"71296a1f-f677-43a6-af3d-80e08ca2f032","timestamp":"2026-09-04T09:18:39.132Z","request_id":"gen-1788513510-NgxCdBUQB2iuookrCFf8"}
