{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"gen-1788513922-rjr6kCmvNOvUaPLLByM2","type":"message","role":"assistant","container":null,"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Done. The workspace format change is implemented and verified. Here's what changed:\n\n## `conanws.yml` format (list-based)\n\n```yaml\npackages:\n  - path: liba\n    ref: liba/0.1\n  - path: libb\n    ref: libb/0.1\n```\n\n**`conan/internal/model/workspace.py`**\n- `packages()` now returns a list of `{path, ref?, output_folder?}` entries instead of a ref-keyed dict.\n- `add(ref, path, output_folder)` writes `path` + `ref` entries, and warns `Package <path> already exists, skipping` when a package is already registered at that path (no duplicates).\n- `remove(path)` finds the entry **by path** (with `next(..., None)` so a missing path raises the intended `ConanException: No editable package to remove from this path` rather than a `StopIteration` crash) and returns the path.\n- `clean()` labels each package by its `ref` when defined, falling back to `path` — e.g. `Removing liba/0.1 output folder: ...` vs `Removing libb output folder: ...`.\n- Paths keep being normalized to Unix separators via `_conan_rel_path()`.\n\n**`conan/api/subapi/workspace.py`** — `packages()` still returns the public `{RecipeReference: {\"path\", \"output_folder\"}}` dict, so all commands (install/build/create/source, graph editables) work unchanged — this is where backward compatibility lives. Each entry's ref is deduced: explicitly from `ref` in the yml, or from the conanfile via `load_conanfile()` when absent. Error handling:\n- `Workspace editable not found: <path>` when the conanfile is missing\n- `Workspace editable reference could not be deduced by <path>/conanfile.py or it is not correctly defined in the conanws.yml file.`\n- `Workspace editable reference '<ref>' already exists.` on duplicate refs across different paths\n- (I narrowed the patch's bare `except:` to `except Exception:` and added the `next()` default — behavior/messages otherwise identical to the reference change.)\n\n**`conan/cli/commands/workspace.py`** — `workspace info` text output renders the list:\n```\npackages\n  - path: ../liba\n    ref: liba/0.1\n```\n`--format=json` emits the raw list entries; ref is omitted when not defined.\n\n**`conan/internal/api/new/workspace.py`** — the `conan new workspace` template now generates the list format with `path` + `ref` per package.\n\n## Verification\n- `test/integration/workspace/test_workspace.py` updated to the new format plus three new tests (paths-only without refs, duplicate references, undeducible reference) — **39/39 pass**\n- Full integration suite: **2844 passed**, 2 failures (`test_export_read_only`, `test_wrong_home_error`) confirmed pre-existing on the clean tree; `test/functional/workspace::test_metabuild` also fails pre-existing (CMake environment)\n- Manual smoke confirmed: duplicate-path skip warning, remove-by-path, both ref-deduction error messages, clean messaging by ref/path fallback, and Unix-normalized relative paths in the saved yml\n\nOne thing to be aware of: custom `conanws.py` subclasses that override `packages()` must now return a **list** of dicts (e.g. `[{\"path\": f, \"ref\": f\"{f}/0.1\"}]`) instead of a ref-keyed dict — this is an intentional contract change for the incubating feature (it's gated behind `CONAN_WORKSPACE_ENABLE=will_break_next`), and the tests reflect it.","citations":[]}],"model":"z-ai/glm-5.3-flash","stop_reason":null,"stop_details":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0,"output_tokens_details":null,"cache_creation_input_tokens":null,"cache_read_input_tokens":null,"cache_creation":null,"inference_geo":null,"server_tool_use":null,"service_tier":null,"speed":"standard"},"provider":"Z.AI","context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a035cbe5-8923-4731-8824-502460b30912","uuid":"3e4cc173-a557-4e98-a5da-fd317824fbd3","timestamp":"2026-09-04T09:25:45.320Z","request_id":"gen-1788513922-rjr6kCmvNOvUaPLLByM2"}
